## 10. Airborne underside redirect (2026-11-14)

- The user reverted the earlier upside-down/front-wheel Redirect experiment. Do not assume that implementation is present or reintroduce its wheel offsets.
- The current Redirect is a separate subclass of `Aerial`; ordinary Aerial behaviour remains the fallback and is otherwise unchanged.
- Shot selection considers Redirect only for a goal-directed aerial candidate when the predicted ball is behind Volt in local coordinates (local y < -150), airborne (z > 250), moving at more than 600 uu/s, and travelling generally toward the opponent goal.
- It also projects the predicted ball trajectory to the opponent goal line. Redirect is selected only when the projected path is near the goal mouth but close to/outside a post, the required correction is modest (at most 35 degrees), and the intercept is reachable within the current time limits.
- Redirect approaches the predicted ball position from above. Its forward axis follows the ball's existing horizontal travel direction; its underside is tilted slightly toward the required lateral correction. The contact target is offset by ball radius plus half the hitbox height.
- Redirect deliberately skips the final dodge. The intended touch is a shallow trajectory correction that preserves most of the ball's existing speed, rather than a powerful shot that kills its momentum.
- The geometry is an initial model, not a validated collision simulation. In-game tests must establish whether the car actually contacts with its underside and whether the ball retains enough speed.
- Untargeted aerial selection remains normal Aerial. Redirect is only selected in the goal-directed `find_shot` path.
- The live branch still contains `wall_approach` and wall-drive selection logic; inspect the live code before any wall-related edit.

